    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Post-radiation epithelioidangiosarcoma</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Post-radiation epithelioid angiosarcoma shows sheets of pleomorphic malignant cells that mimic carcinoma. The vasoformative nature is recognised at the advancing tumour front where anastomosing and slit-like spaces are lined by malignant cells. Immunohistochemistry confirmed endothelial differentiation. There was a history of breast carcinoma with radiation treatment 10 years prior to the development of the current tumour.</p>",
    "source": "<p>SGH Pathology</p>",
